                <pb facs="0903" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0090/1728: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-03">August 3,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received August 3—5:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4695. American interests Japan. Department’s 1739, July 24 transmitted Legation
                    Tokyo [by] Swiss Foreign Office. Received simultaneously from Legation Tokyo
                    telegram expressing fear decision Japanese authorities refuse repatriation Guam
                    internees final. To avoid delay Japanese-American exchange, Gorgé desires know
                    whether may submit Japanese Foreign Office new list Americans as substitutes
                    Guam internees in case latter unauthorized leave Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
